{"name":"field glasses","about":"Made by tools/battle-models (prop). Metres; x forward, y right, z up. A battle model: `part` says which part each point belongs to; `parts` are the parts (parent, pivot, axis of turning, way of sliding); `sockets` are named places for flash, smoke, fire and wake; `clips` move the parts. Turns: +t degrees about an axis carries p to p cos t + (axis x p) sin t + axis (axis . p)(1 - cos t), about the part's pivot. Paints: 0 upper, 1 upper2, 2 shade, 3 track, 4 rubber, 5 steel, 6 bright, 7 wood, 8 canvas, 9 glass, 10 black, 11 rust, 12 lamp, 13 white, 14 red, 15 yellow, 16 blue, 17 leather, 18 torn, 19 rope, 20 cloth, 21 skin, 22 brass, 23 webbing, 24 bakelite, 25 wire, 26 zinc. The tank commander's field glasses (binoculars_prop.py, from the studio's crew/props/binoculars.glb): the origin between the eyepieces, the barrels along +x. Drawn where a tankers' clip's `props` track `binoculars` puts them (t, x, y, z, qw, qx, qy, qz, shown; the clip's root frame, 30 a second), while `shown` is 1.","kind":"prop","colours":["60664A","4C513B","3B3F2D","37322E","202022","4A4C4A","8C8E90","8C6B47","6B6847","1B2A33","101112","4A3226","2B3336","E6E2D8","A82020","C9A227","2F4A7A","5C4430","241D1A","8A7A5A","807A56","C49A7A","9A8448","6E6A4C","2C2B2A","34302A","7E8078"],"paint_names":["upper","upper2","shade","track","rubber","steel","bright","wood","canvas","glass","black","rust","lamp","white","red","yellow","blue","leather","torn","rope","cloth","skin","brass","webbing","bakelite","wire","zinc"],"near":{"points":[-0.005,-0.0746,0.0038,-0.005,-0.0746,0.0038,-0.005,-0.0713,0.0106,-0.005,-0.0713,0.0106,-0.005,-0.0654,0.0153,-0.005,-0.0654,0.0153,-0.005,-0.058,0.017,-0.005,-0.058,0.017,-0.005,-0.0506,0.0153,-0.005,-0.0506,0.0153,-0.005,-0.0447,0.0106,-0.005,-0.0447,0.0106,-0.005,-0.0414,0.0038,-0.005,-0.0414,0.0038,-0.005,-0.0414,-0.0038,-0.005,-0.0414,-0.0038,-0.005,-0.0447,-0.0106,-0.005,-0.0447,-0.0106,-0.005,-0.0506,-0.0153,-0.005,-0.0506,-0.0153,-0.